coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\nThe distance from any point to the origin on the given surface equals $3.$ On the other hand, $\\theta $ and $ϕ$ vary arbitrarily in their respective domains. \n\nTherefore, the spherical polar equation of the surface is $\\rho =3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135247/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "133f6b90-4074-5860-9b89-16b59c5613bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection/b1351b8d6e4b1f60c445722c5aab2f3e1a56009d234588b4f56554f9bba327b8" :answer/id #uuid "da52c0aa-e322-53ed-9ff8-1b50d64089b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A sphere" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection/d75c85b2503ed0099aad81b1b67dae5234ba71bcf5b076be8cdc6fdfefdfbe33" :answer/id #uuid "f8c5ee14-31b6-5e32-bd32-c103ca23e536" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipsoid" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection/e3bc01c1a7cc4eaaa3d0fec3c0eb87ff9cb3bf03f2891a742d43b82797869ffc" :answer/id #uuid "0b12f108-5a9c-51e5-90f3-31ed335582c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circular cylinder" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection/629edb33ca1a99b9b321b4aa6f9cd868354c57a10386e13007d4b875cd623645" :answer/id #uuid "d48090ef-223c-5060-8e26-b55a1d772ae0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A half-line" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection/c42687c1e0e0b1f1d69a99bb36f784671f2be77b295e7dc563f9366ef570bdd1" :answer/id #uuid "2f16f454-f67c-5c6f-a643-192706c88440" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A half-cone" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5342f24-aeb7-586e-bce3-442a1af3ab4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-135300/selection/b1351b8d6e4b1f60c445722c5aab2f3e1a56009d234588b4f56554f9bba327b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-135300/selection/b1351b8d6e4b1f60c445722c5aab2f3e1a56009d234588b4f56554f9bba327b8" "q-135300/selection/d75c85b2503ed0099aad81b1b67dae5234ba71bcf5b076be8cdc6fdfefdfbe33" "q-135300/selection/e3bc01c1a7cc4eaaa3d0fec3c0eb87ff9cb3bf03f2891a742d43b82797869ffc" "q-135300/selection/629edb33ca1a99b9b321b4aa6f9cd868354c57a10386e13007d4b875cd623645" "q-135300/selection/c42687c1e0e0b1f1d69a99bb36f784671f2be77b295e7dc563f9366ef570bdd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135300" :question/id #uuid "88fdcb72-76af-50c0-96fa-8648d47767d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-135300" :question/problem "What surface is defined by the equation $\\rho =\\pi $ in spherical polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our equation:\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\pi \n$$\n\nThis equation specifies that for any point on the surface, the distance from the point to the origin must equal $\\pi .$ On the other hand, $\\theta $ and $ϕ$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains. \n\nTherefore, our surface is a sphere.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038412/assets/3775fdcb48fd015097b484b6d5ebaefcecd4ef10298cb18b34226a8eae1be1ef.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-135300/selec